{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QuantumPlanckConstant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QuantumPlanckConstant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.planck_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.planck_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-planck-constant.lean#L49-L54","doc":"At classicality (`q = 1`), the quantum Planck constant vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumPlanckConstantSibling_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumPlanckConstantSibling_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-planck-constant.lean#L41-L47","doc":"The quantum Planck constant is strictly less than one (`ℏ_q < 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumPlanckConstantSibling_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumPlanckConstantSibling_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-planck-constant.lean#L31-L39","doc":"The quantum Planck constant is non-negative (`0 ≤ ℏ_q`), since `q(p) ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantumPlanckConstantSibling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantumPlanckConstantSibling","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-planck-constant.lean#L21-L29","doc":"**Quantum Planck constant**: `ℏ_q(p) = 1 − q(p)⁻¹`.\n\nA field `M → [0, 1)`.  At classicality `q → 1` we get `ℏ_q → 0`;\nin the deep-quantum regime `q → ∞` we get `ℏ_q → 1`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-planck-constant}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}